# Multi-Platform Development Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines apply to multi-platform development, enabling maximum code sharing between mobile, web, and desktop while optimizing the user experience for each specific platform.

## Best Practices
- Use separate entry point structure: main_mobile.dart, main_web.dart, main_desktop.dart
- Separate platform-specific logic using conditional imports
- Implement responsive design rather than adaptive design where possible
- Leverage LayoutBuilder and MediaQuery widgets for responsive UI
- Use factory patterns to create platform-specific widgets and services
- Prioritize shared code repositories, only separating when necessary
- Use Flutter Platform Channels for platform-specific features
- Maintain consistent APIs across platforms, even if implementations differ

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize entry point structure:
  ```
  lib/
    ├── main.dart              # Common entry point or default mobile
    ├── main_mobile.dart       # Mobile entry point
    ├── main_web.dart          # Web entry point
    ├── main_desktop.dart      # Desktop entry point
    ├── presentation/
    │   ├── widgets/
    │   │   ├── common/        # Shared widgets across platforms
    │   │   ├── mobile/        # Mobile-specific widgets
    │   │   ├── web/           # Web-specific widgets
    │   │   └── desktop/       # Desktop-specific widgets
    └── core/
        ├── platform/
        │   ├── platform_info.dart      # Platform detection utilities
        │   └── platform_widgets.dart   # Platform-specific widget factories
  ```

- Use factories for platform-specific widgets:
  ```dart
  abstract class PlatformButton {
    factory PlatformButton() {
      if (kIsWeb) return WebButton();
      if (Platform.isAndroid || Platform.isIOS) return MobileButton();
      return DesktopButton();
    }
    
    Widget build(BuildContext context, String label, VoidCallback onPressed);
  }
  ```

## Entry Point Structure
- Organization of main.dart and platform-specific mains:
  ```dart
  // main.dart
  void main() {
    // Common initialization
    WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
    // Platform detection and forwarding
    if (kIsWeb) {
      webMain();
    } else if (Platform.isAndroid || Platform.isIOS) {
      mobileMain();
    } else {
      desktopMain();
    }
  }
  ```

- Platform-specific mains:
  ```dart
  // main_mobile.dart
  void mobileMain() {
    // Mobile-specific initialization
    initializeMobileServices();
    runApp(const AppEntry(platform: PlatformType.mobile));
  }
  ```

## Platform-Specific Configuration
- Managing platform-specific dependencies:
  ```yaml
  # pubspec.yaml
  dependencies:
    # Common dependencies
    flutter:
      sdk: flutter
    
    # Mobile-specific
    flutter_local_notifications: ^19.0.0
    
    # Web-specific
    url_launcher_web: ^2.0.0
    
    # Desktop-specific
    window_size:
      git:
        url: https://github.com/google/flutter-desktop-embedding.git
        path: plugins/window_size
  ```

## Responsive Design Guidelines
- Using LayoutBuilder and MediaQuery for responsive UI:
  ```dart
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return LayoutBuilder(
      builder: (context, constraints) {
        if (constraints.maxWidth > 1200) {
          return DesktopLayout(child: content);
        } else if (constraints.maxWidth > 600) {
          return TabletLayout(child: content);
        } else {
          return MobileLayout(child: content);
        }
      },
    );
  }
  ```

- Using FlexBuilder for adaptive widgets:
  ```dart
  Widget buildUserList() {
    return FlexBuilder(
      mobile: (context) => ListView.builder(/* mobile config */),
      desktop: (context) => GridView.builder(/* desktop config */),
      tablet: (context) => ListView.builder(/* tablet config */),
    );
  }
  ```

## Service Locator Configuration
- Configuring dependency injection by platform:
  ```dart
  void configureDependencies(PlatformType platform) {
    // Common dependencies
    getIt.registerSingleton<NetworkService>(NetworkServiceImpl());
    
    // Platform specific dependencies
    switch (platform) {
      case PlatformType.mobile:
        getIt.registerSingleton<NotificationService>(MobileNotificationService());
        break;
      case PlatformType.web:
        getIt.registerSingleton<NotificationService>(WebNotificationService());
        break;
      case PlatformType.desktop:
        getIt.registerSingleton<NotificationService>(DesktopNotificationService());
        break;
    }
  }
  ```

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Write platform-agnostic tests when possible
- Use mocks for platform-specific services
- Write golden tests for UI across different screen sizes
- Test user experience on all target platforms
- Use device lab or device farm for automated testing
- Monitor and analyze performance metrics across platforms
